# AscendNPU-IR Docs Governance Rule

Use this rule when updating user/developer docs or when behavior changes require documentation updates.

## 1) Documentation ownership map

- architecture and introduction:
  - `docs/source/en/introduction/**`
- user options and debugging:
  - `docs/source/en/user_guide/compile_option.md`
  - `docs/source/en/user_guide/debug_option.md`
- developer internals:
  - `docs/source/en/developer_guide/**`
- contribution expectations:
  - `docs/source/en/contributing_guide/contribute.md`

Mirror in `docs/source/zh_cn/**` if project convention requires bilingual parity.

## 2) Update checklist for behavior changes

1. identify user-visible impact (flags, defaults, supported cases, diagnostics)
2. update user guide text and examples first
3. update developer internals for implementation/path changes
4. verify pass/option names match actual CLI and code
5. ensure no stale examples remain in nearby pages

## 3) Quality checklist

- terminology is consistent across architecture/options/features docs
- headings and section depth follow existing style
- commands/options are copy-paste valid
- docs avoid claiming unsupported behavior

## 4) Change classification guidance

- option default change:
  - update compile option docs and migration notes.
- new pass or pipeline gate:
  - update developer guide and option mapping docs.
- new feature workflow:
  - add playbook-style implementation and validation steps.

## 5) Done criteria

- all impacted docs are updated with consistent terminology
- examples and command snippets align with current implementation
- bilingual mirror performed when required by project process
